the clark county school district  welcomes back most staff to its  buildings today and for some it's the  first time stepping on campus  since the start of distance education  and that was a year ago  eight news now reporter kristen drummond  live in the newsroom with the latest on  this adjustment kristen  denise yes educators returning as part  of the hybrid transition plan  teachers will use this week to prepare  for students in grades  6 9 and 12 coming back next monday  i did try to visit a high school in  person but ccsd does not want reporters  in buildings especially now since  parents are not even allowed on campuses  for safety reasons but  a few school principals shared photos  with me showing staff  back and the classrooms this is las  vegas high school right here in the east  valley the pictures show  desks set up already and space depart  for social distancing  the principal tells me majority of his  staff came back on campus today  he adds there's a buzz of positivity as  colleagues see each other again  in person despite the circumstances  things are  far from normal but  it's just the fact that we see each  other's cars now in the parking lot  and we cross each other's paths like we  normally would  that just just charges up  our energy at spring valley high school  in the southwest valley staff received  welcome back swag bags as a sign of  support from the administration  one of the gifts included a pin with the  school's mascot wearing a mask  the principal tells me about 98 percent  of his faculty return today  most teachers will work from school  buildings this week  unless they made a request to work  remotely because of health concerns  now coming up at six two teachers talk  with me about their adjustment today  including what it's like to be back  after a year of teaching from home  reporting live in the newsroom kristen  drummond 8 news now
 

